source	D. Hume, Enquiry concerning Human Understanding (1748), sect. X
text	Project Gutenberg ebook 9662, https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/9662
class	inference
at	S6	There must, therefore, be a uniform experience against every miraculous event
fault	question-begging: that experience against miracles is uniform is drawn from the definition of a miracle, which presupposes that no testimony to one is part of experience
reference	J. Earman, Hume's Abject Failure (2000); W. Paley, Evidences of Christianity (1794)
